==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}}, {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|percussion}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|percussiō||striking}}, from {{m|la|percutiō||I strike}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/pɚˈkʌʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|percussions}}

# {{label|en|countable}} The [[collision]] of two [[bodies]] in order to produce a [[sound]].
# {{label|en|countable}} The sound so produced.
# {{label|en|countable}} The [[detonation]] of a [[percussion cap]] in a [[firearm]].
# {{label|en|medicine}} The [[tapping]] of the [[body]] as an aid to [[medical]] [[diagnosis]].
# {{label|en|music}} The section of an [[orchestra]] or band containing [[percussion instrument]]s; such instruments considered as a group; in bands, may be separate from [[drum kit]]s.
# {{label|en|engineering}} The repeated striking of an object to break or shape it, as in percussion drilling.

